soon as I lose one of those big clients  I start looking for others long-term  clients is probably one of the secrets  to making this work for you and of  course this is where the other crucial  aspects of running an online business  comes in if you're going to do this in  the long term  you need to be good at what you do need  to be reliable you need to stick to  deadlines maintain communication with  your clients and ensure the businesses  know they can rely on you you're good to  my wife I will stay with you yes that's  one of the biggest problems when trying  to find online freelancers and that's  where you'll stand out against the crowd  it's the only way you'll get clients to  want to stick around and the only way  you can build your contacts list and  it's the only way you'll get recommended  to other clients too and another way you  can benefit from this kind of work from  this gig economy is by not necessarily  being a full time freelancer but by  earning money on the side so if you've  got a job you like but you're not  earning quite enough money then why not  do some work in the evenings on the  commute home even you can start to  supplement your income that way once  again it's just seeing that your income  isn't tied to your salary salary income  aren't the same and income and wealth  certainly aren't the same and that's how  you need to think if you want to design  the lifestyle you want and the business  that you want  likewise you can also use freelancing  and gigging as a way to transition  between jobs and in particular if you  lose a job or something then this is a  great way to tide you over until you  find another job and if you're  interested in becoming a freelancer or  entering the gig economy and you  currently work a 9 to 5 then the way to  do that is to first do a little bit of  work in the evenings or even on your  commute home and then just sell it  online when you get back and then to  increase that gradually eventually might  be able to drop a day of work in your  office maybe work four days a week maybe  eventually go part-time and then only  once you've got a stable income and  you're sure it works can you give up  your full-time job this isn't a risky  venture you don't have to just quit your  job I'm quitting and then hope you find  the work online you can make sure it  works and then quit your job although to  be honest there is a lot of work out  there as long as you are skilled do  develop the skills as long as you're  dedicated as long as you work hard and  then you put yourself out there you know  how to market yourself and sell those  skills then there's enough work out  there that I think you really don't need  to worry actually if you've you've asked  in the past that I talked about some of  the books I have here beside me  certainly there are a lot of great books  that I can recommend if you want to get  into freelancing and working online one  such book is the 4-hour workweek by Tim  Ferriss  that's a fantastic one it tells you how  to better manage your work-life balance  how to lower the amount of time you're  working whilst getting more profit from  that time and fortunately that's a book  that's missing from my collection right  now as I lent it out and never got it  back the bastards another great one that  I do have here is the personal MBA by  Josh Kaufman this is an MBA in a book so  it attempts to teach you everything you  need to know about running a business  and it does a pretty admirable job of  that I highly recommend this one as a  way to learn the basics I also picked up  a few tips from Richard Branson's book  but more excitingly and more importantly  stay tuned because I've just signed a  contract to write my next book which is  going to be all about navigating the gig  economy and working online as a  freelancer so sometime next year that  will be available and I'll be sure to  update you about that then so yeah  really the aim of this video was just to  demonstrate that you can start to view  your work and your lifestyle slightly  differently not so quicker this is work  this is  because sometimes you can work on  projects that end up earning money and  you don't have to say I'm gonna work  these set hours you can work  whichever hours you want to put out  throughout the day spread out throughout  the week I've actually ended up taking  Monday's off and working harder Tuesday  to Friday I use Mondays now just to work  on the bionaire which I believe in the  future could earn me a fair amount of  money possibly a full-time income so  this is the way you've got to think you  don't have to be black and white this is  what I work this is what I'm done this  is my salary instead you can pick and  choose jobs manage them as you like deal  with those difficult clients get rid of  the ones that are too difficult find the  ones that are long-term develop your  skills and then that way you can design  what you want work to look like you can  pursue the things you find interesting  you can create the time to spend with  family friends hobbies and for me  personally I just think is a better way  of living and it's not for everyone but  maybe you do as well and hopefully this  videos inspired you to at least give it  a try let me know in the comments down  below if you have any questions or if  you'd like to see more videos on this  topic thanks a ton for watching guys  fans video useful please leave a like  please share around  like I say comment down below subscribe  to the channel if you want more on this  on productivity on technology but also  fitness bodybuilding biohacking  transhumanism nootropics all the usual  stuff if that sounds good then thanks a  ton for watching and I'll see you next  time bye for now
 

